WEBVTT

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:05.540
Are you going to throw us

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:09.730
and everything we've been through
together away to be alone?

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.690
Choose, Kouta.

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:17.970
You guys or myself?

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:33.090
The Magic of Friends

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:34.760
It was... really painful.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:44.000
Yuu, Shunsuke, Ryo,
President... you all sparkled,

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:47.040
but I was the only one that didn't.

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:52.490
You all shine so brightly that
no one can even see me.

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:57.990
So I even thought that you were in my way.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:05.200
We're friends, so how could
I even think like that?

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:08.830
It was so painful.

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:11.500
Kouta-kun...

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:18.220
If it's always going to be this
painful being with everyone,

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:21.010
then...

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:21.930
Wait.

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:26.060
Remember what you said back then?

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:29.060
I'm ready, you can approach me!

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:33.700
The person who said that I could approach
them shouldn't be trying to be alone!

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:37.120
Kouta-kun, I...

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:40.520
I think you're the one who is even
more shameful for saying such things

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:43.250
when someone who has looked
after you has collapsed.

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:48.980
I'm not such a shameful person to leave
a friend alone when they're in pain!

00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:52.630
Don't overestimate us, Kouta.

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:55.190
No matter how perfect you are, it's too much.

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:57.830
And it makes us feel lonely.

00:01:57.830 --> 00:01:59.660
Because we're not perfect.

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:03.310
You were the one who told me
it's okay not to be perfect.

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:12.810
Shunsuke, Ryo, President...

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:19.870
But I...

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:21.220
Can't decide?

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:24.470
Of course you can't.

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:28.980
Saying you don't want to be with
us because you can't sparkle

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:36.350
is nothing more than the whining
of a selfish, spoiled child!

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:39.880
Shut up!

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:45.750
Why do you have to be the one to say that?!

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:50.980
You were the one who couldn't
say anything to Yuri-chan!

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:52.610
Yeah, that's right!

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:55.800
Despite being older, I was afraid of her,

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:58.010
so I couldn't really tell her anything!

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:00.550
But I couldn't help it!

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:02.450
I was just a kid!

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:06.090
That's right! Me, you, all of us are.

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:09.710
We've been together all this time,
so figure that much out, you idiot!

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:11.250
Who's the idiot?

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:12.130
You are!

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:15.540
We didn't realize you were
hurting because we're just kids!

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:17.760
And we hurt you,

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.090
I'm so sorry!

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:30.370
Did you not have fun?

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:36.710
Were you really feeling nothing but
pain all the time we were together?!

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:39.780
Of course I had fun!

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:43.810
I talked a lot with you guys after school!

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:45.880
I went to Gift Gate for the first time!

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:47.520
And I went to Puroland!

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.390
Had the training camp at the beach.

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:53.880
The fireworks and the starry sky that
I saw with you guys were really pretty!

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:55.070
This was...

00:03:56.350 --> 00:04:01.470
This was the first time I'd ever
had so much fun in school!

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:01.470
Well, then!

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:05.960
Don't go off on your own.

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:11.330
Choose us.

00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:13.300
Yuu...

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:19.920
After telling me to choose...

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:25.560
This is messed up.

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:29.620
Yeah, Yuu is pretty messed up,

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:33.250
but this is one time I agree with him.

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:35.650
Choose me, Kouta.

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:39.500
I won't hold myself back like a kid anymore.

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:41.190
Shunsuke...

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:44.300
Choose me, too, Kouta-kun!

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:48.940
I want to become even better friends with you!

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:52.270
I'm going to do what I want, too, Kouta.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:54.930
I want you to choose me, too.

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:57.450
Ryo, President...

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:09.150
Don't say such selfish things.

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:14.660
Besides, whenever we're together,
I end up feeling miserable.

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:16.380
What's wrong with being selfish?

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:18.090
What do I care about your feelings?

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:23.380
I, we, want to be with you!

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:28.210
There was totally another
way he could've said that.

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:30.220
But this is more his style.

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:33.210
Yeah, he's selfish and willful

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:35.920
but there is no limit to his kindness.

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:41.360
But I have to do it by myself—

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:43.110
That's what I'm talking about!

00:05:44.290 --> 00:05:47.110
Why are you obsessed with
doing things on your own?

00:05:47.510 --> 00:05:49.240
Because I promised...

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:52.140
You know, we've tagged along with you so far,

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:54.420
but even we're starting to feel the same way.

00:05:55.010 --> 00:05:57.380
But we're not enough.

00:05:57.380 --> 00:06:00.090
Yes, it has to be the five of us.

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:01.840
Get it?

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:06.010
We want to sparkle <i>with</i> you, Kouta!

00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:08.780
With me?

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:14.490
<i>Is that what you really want to do, Kou-chan?</i>

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:24.410
Well?

00:06:24.970 --> 00:06:29.250
I-It is. I want to sparkle
like everybody else.

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:30.820
Of course,

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:35.770
but is it really just for Purin and I to see?

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:42.500
I-It really is! I wouldn't
lie to you and Purin.

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:44.110
Yes, of course not,

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:47.870
but I wonder if you're lying to yourself.

00:06:47.870 --> 00:06:50.090
Huh? Lying to myself?

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:53.300
Yes, lying to yourself.

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:07.260
I wanted to sparkle together.

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:09.130
With who?

00:07:10.710 --> 00:07:12.410
My precious friends.

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:18.560
That's right.

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:25.010
I wanted... to sparkle with everyone all along.

00:07:26.910 --> 00:07:28.520
That was all it was.

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:36.460
There is nothing you can't do, Kou-chan.

00:07:41.150 --> 00:07:42.100
Grandma!

00:07:55.570 --> 00:07:57.650
I want to sparkle with everyone, too.

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:02.200
But I can't give you anything.

00:08:03.930 --> 00:08:06.130
Just being with us is enough.

00:08:07.490 --> 00:08:10.220
Just being with you?

00:08:12.210 --> 00:08:13.010
Yeah.

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:26.630
<i>We can be happy just by being together</i>

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:32.990
<i>That is the magic of friends</i>

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:39.350
<i>If we join hands, our spirit will surge through us</i>

00:08:39.350 --> 00:08:45.630
<i>And we can all smile!</i>

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:53.420
The magic of friends...

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:05.200
That's my...

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:06.810
Don't leave him behind again.

00:09:09.010 --> 00:09:09.810
Okay.

00:09:18.130 --> 00:09:21.250
<i>We're going to start over again from here.</i>

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:26.590
<i>Our youth, as the Sanrio Boys!</i>

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:40.090
Hasegawa?

00:09:40.090 --> 00:09:41.200
Sugami-sensei?

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:43.100
Don't run in the halls.

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:44.600
Yes, sir!

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:46.760
Good luck with the preparations.

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:50.280
Thanks, we're pushing through the final hurdle.

00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:55.280
Sorry I'm late guys.

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:57.380
What's the matter?

00:09:57.380 --> 00:09:59.680
N-N-N-N-Nothing's the matter.

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:01.910
Yuu-kun, you're being ridiculously suspicious.

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:06.110
Sorry, we were having
a bit of a secret conversation.

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:09.730
That's way too honest, President.

00:10:09.730 --> 00:10:12.730
Okay, well, just let me join in next time.

00:10:15.150 --> 00:10:17.350
You've gotten stronger somehow, haven't you?

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:21.160
Anyway, today's our last run-through, right?

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:22.470
We gotta focus our energy.

00:10:22.900 --> 00:10:25.770
R-Right, tomorrow is the real deal, after all.

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:30.770
Kinda feels like it passed by in a flash.

00:10:31.260 --> 00:10:33.290
But we had lots of help.

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:36.250
We can't let their feelings go to waste.

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:39.680
Yeah, they said they'd even help
out backstage during the show,

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:40.670
and the music—

00:10:41.380 --> 00:10:42.530
The music?!

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:48.000
Crap! I completely forgot
to search for new music!

00:10:48.630 --> 00:10:50.980
What are we gonna do? We
won't make it in time!

00:10:49.010 --> 00:10:51.610
Well, Kouta-kun, about that...

00:10:50.550 --> 00:10:52.420
I heard your conversation!

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:57.140
I'm the only one you can
depend on in the end, after all.

00:10:57.140 --> 00:10:58.600
Sorry, Macchi.

00:10:58.600 --> 00:11:01.050
I don't have time to play with you right now.

00:11:01.770 --> 00:11:04.170
That was harsher than ever before.

00:11:04.170 --> 00:11:06.720
But what is with this
strange sense of security?

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:08.810
Jeez, Macchi, you're just confusing things.

00:11:09.810 --> 00:11:11.450
Here you are, Mizuno,

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:13.930
the music we promised.

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:16.690
It was down to the wire, but we
managed to make it in time.

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:18.620
Thank you, we're saved!

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:20.160
Did you say music just now?

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:22.650
What, you didn't know, Hase?

00:11:24.130 --> 00:11:26.130
Mizuno asked me for help.

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:29.910
He asked if the light music
club could make some songs.

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:32.160
Yuu asked you?

00:11:32.910 --> 00:11:33.920
Please!

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:35.920
Sure!

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:41.050
Well, I didn't do it all by myself.
I had a bit of help.

00:11:41.660 --> 00:11:43.130
Sorry, Macchi.

00:11:43.540 --> 00:11:46.330
This whole time I seriously thought
you were just in charge of the air guitar

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:48.560
or that it was the fashionable
light music club.

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:50.930
That innocent expression is too much.

00:11:50.930 --> 00:11:54.080
I do play an instrument, y'know!
It's the light music club after all!

00:11:54.080 --> 00:11:56.140
Oh, but what about you Tsucchi?

00:11:56.480 --> 00:12:00.240
I can play some instruments,
so I helped out a bit.

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:01.750
It was pretty fun.

00:12:02.180 --> 00:12:06.430
I definitely won't be surprised
at what you can do anymore.

00:12:07.090 --> 00:12:09.830
Kouta, let's give it a listen.

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:11.770
Yeah, sure.

00:12:11.770 --> 00:12:14.270
Macchi, Tsucchi, thank you!

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:21.760
That's our Hase, isn't it?

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:23.340
That's our Hase.

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:29.680
<b>Hijirikawa High School Cultural Festival</b>

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:31.930
<i>The Hijirikawa High School
festival is now open.</i>

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:31.930
Food and Drink Booth

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:31.930
Yakisoba

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:34.690
Authentic Taste! Okonomiyaki

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:35.600
<i>Please refer to the flyer for the
times of each performance.</i>

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:38.040
It's iffy.

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:39.140
Iffy?

00:12:39.140 --> 00:12:41.190
Okay, it's a special gift for my
adorable underclassman.

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:43.330
I don't want it, you're
just pushing it off on me!

00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:45.270
Hey now, don't go getting too riled up.

00:12:43.330 --> 00:12:44.850
It's fine, it's fine, here.

00:12:44.850 --> 00:12:45.980
I said I don't want it.

00:12:47.230 --> 00:12:48.250
Yuri!

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:50.870
This sucks. Why'd I have
to run into you here?

00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:54.850
Did you come here by any chance
to support your big brother, Yuri-chan?

00:12:54.850 --> 00:12:58.080
Of course I didn't! Stop saying gross things!

00:12:59.970 --> 00:13:01.760
Oh, Yuri-chan. There you are!

00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:04.960
So immature.

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:07.800
Wait, Yuri!

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:09.810
Food Ticket

00:13:08.440 --> 00:13:09.810
A parting gift from your big brother.

00:13:10.410 --> 00:13:12.650
Are you sure?

00:13:12.650 --> 00:13:14.450
Yeah, just don't eat too much.

00:13:14.450 --> 00:13:16.360
I don't eat that much anyway.

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:19.640
But I guess I'll hang on to them.

00:13:19.640 --> 00:13:21.320
Okay, have fun.

00:13:21.640 --> 00:13:23.510
I'll try anyway.

00:13:24.460 --> 00:13:25.700
See you later, then.

00:13:29.270 --> 00:13:31.200
C-Come on, let's go, Ma-kun.

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:35.130
"Later," she said.

00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:37.800
Looks like Yuri came to see the play, too.

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:41.810
I-It doesn't really matter if
she's here to see it or not.

00:13:41.810 --> 00:13:43.630
And that's what makes you a tsundere-type.

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:45.670
You've really been extra bratty lately.

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:48.310
Stop it, come on.

00:13:46.750 --> 00:13:50.810
Putting that aside, I think it's
time we enjoyed the festival, too.

00:13:52.460 --> 00:13:54.940
Man, this is so much fun.

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:57.810
Would this be the Kittyful
thing you say, Shushu?

00:13:57.810 --> 00:14:00.170
This is why you are hopeless.

00:14:00.170 --> 00:14:02.590
You don't understand
the spirit of Kittyful at all.

00:14:02.590 --> 00:14:05.320
Seriously, what is Kittyful though, really?

00:14:07.090 --> 00:14:08.590
So this is where you've been, Ryo!

00:14:10.970 --> 00:14:11.870
Dad?

00:14:12.090 --> 00:14:13.330
Dad?

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:16.500
Yes, and you all are?

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:18.670
Th-They're my friends!

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:21.040
Are they now? I see, I see!

00:14:21.300 --> 00:14:22.660
I'm Ryo's father.

00:14:22.660 --> 00:14:23.710
Ah, hello.

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:28.830
Well, I'm surprised. This is the first time
Ryo's ever introduced me to his friends.

00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:29.970
Hey, stop it, Dad!

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:31.000
It's a pleasure.

00:14:31.360 --> 00:14:34.310
We have been able to experience
various things thanks to Nishimiya-kun.

00:14:34.670 --> 00:14:36.640
Even though he was a bit of a brat at first...

00:14:37.280 --> 00:14:38.000
I guess he still is.

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:39.190
Dang it, Yuu-kun!

00:14:40.490 --> 00:14:41.800
That's great though.

00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:44.950
This means you can make
lots of friends in London, too.

00:14:48.270 --> 00:14:51.540
Ryo isn't very good at being around people,

00:14:51.900 --> 00:14:54.050
so I was a bit worried about him.

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:56.790
Now I'm relieved.

00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:57.800
Dad!

00:14:59.350 --> 00:15:02.210
I'm sorry, I didn't say
anything until now, but...

00:15:03.470 --> 00:15:05.590
I'm not going to London.

00:15:06.040 --> 00:15:08.810
Huh? Ryo, what's this all of a sudden?

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:11.480
I want to stay here.

00:15:11.480 --> 00:15:13.710
I want to stay in Japan where my friends are.

00:15:13.710 --> 00:15:17.170
But you can just make
friends in London, right?

00:15:17.170 --> 00:15:19.410
I'm sure you can now.

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:21.580
Yeah, I probably could.

00:15:22.490 --> 00:15:23.480
But...

00:15:26.640 --> 00:15:28.450
I would rather be with them—

00:15:29.230 --> 00:15:34.360
Kouta-kun, Yuu-kun, Shun-san, and Senpai.

00:15:35.010 --> 00:15:36.310
But...

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:45.810
It seems you've lost, dear.

00:15:45.810 --> 00:15:48.490
Well, we kind of figured this would happen.

00:15:48.490 --> 00:15:52.630
Sugar's been so much happier
everyday since around May.

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:53.690
Nee-san...

00:15:54.190 --> 00:15:55.680
You all, too?

00:15:56.050 --> 00:15:58.520
Which means, if my Sugar isn't going,

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:00.300
then I'm not going to London either.

00:16:00.300 --> 00:16:01.490
Same for me.

00:16:01.490 --> 00:16:02.260
Me, too.

00:16:02.260 --> 00:16:03.190
Then Mama's staying, too.

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:06.840
We can finally all live
together as a family, though.

00:16:06.840 --> 00:16:10.740
Ryo, you said yourself that you didn't
have any fond memories of Japan.

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:16.090
Things are different now.

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:23.260
I'll be able to make lots of really fun
memories by staying here with them!

00:16:23.260 --> 00:16:24.370
I'm sure of it!

00:16:51.310 --> 00:16:53.800
Please take care of my son.

00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:54.770
Dad!

00:16:55.970 --> 00:16:57.140
Please leave it to us.

00:17:01.220 --> 00:17:03.580
By the way, Ryo-chan, are you okay on time?

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:05.960
Yes, indeed! It's my Sugar's big performance!

00:17:06.560 --> 00:17:07.660
That's right!

00:17:07.990 --> 00:17:12.050
All right, let's show them the
greatest performance of their lives!

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:13.990
Yeah, let's go you guys!

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:16.260
Good luck, Ryo-chan!

00:17:15.850 --> 00:17:17.840
Break a leg, Sugar!

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:17.840
Okay, I will!

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:23.730
Hurry up, guys!

00:17:25.750 --> 00:17:26.550
That hurt.

00:17:27.460 --> 00:17:30.370
S-Sorry! I'm kind of in a hurry.

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:54.070
<i>This is the Sanriio Military Academy.</i>

00:17:54.870 --> 00:17:56.890
<i>This is where our story begins</i>

00:17:56.890 --> 00:18:00.770
<i>when five young men, born and
raised in different places, meet.</i>

00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:06.770
I am Sei, prince of the Cinnaamoll Empire.

00:18:07.170 --> 00:18:10.390
I am Yuucisus, also a knight candidate.

00:18:11.020 --> 00:18:14.530
I am the crown prince of
the Kikiira Kingdom, Riyon.

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:15.790
Shun.

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:18.350
I am the knight candidate
who serves his highness Riyon

00:18:18.350 --> 00:18:20.910
and representative of the Kittyful family.

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:24.120
I'm Koural, a nobleman from the Pomrin Duchy!

00:18:24.630 --> 00:18:25.920
It's a pleasure to meet you all!

00:18:31.850 --> 00:18:34.000
<i>This is fun,</i>

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:37.410
<i>but I'm sure it's because
we're all here together.</i>

00:18:39.770 --> 00:18:42.640
My native land of Mymelolle was
destroyed by your great nations!

00:18:43.130 --> 00:18:45.730
I had been living to avenge my country...

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:52.250
If only I hadn't met you,
I could have gotten my revenge!

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:54.330
Yuucisus...

00:19:01.990 --> 00:19:04.800
<i>I had closed off my heart for a long time,</i>

00:19:05.770 --> 00:19:07.660
<i>but everyone set me free.</i>

00:19:13.030 --> 00:19:17.080
This is a Kittyful family problem
and it has nothing to do with any of you.

00:19:17.810 --> 00:19:19.910
But even so, will you help me?

00:19:20.460 --> 00:19:21.670
Of course!

00:19:23.410 --> 00:19:26.620
<i>I was afraid to get close to others
but everyone gave my weak back</i>

00:19:27.740 --> 00:19:29.230
<i>a gentle push.</i>

00:19:36.120 --> 00:19:39.080
I admit it... I'm weak.

00:19:39.690 --> 00:19:43.720
But if you all will look out for me, I...

00:19:43.720 --> 00:19:45.030
Go, Riyon!

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:52.040
<i>Everyone gave me the courage and change</i>

00:19:52.690 --> 00:19:53.980
<i>to face my own weakness.</i>

00:20:00.890 --> 00:20:01.930
You!

00:20:02.550 --> 00:20:05.180
It can't be, Riyon?!

00:20:06.940 --> 00:20:08.370
It's all right.

00:20:08.370 --> 00:20:11.830
We will break up this marriage
engagement that you do not desire.

00:20:19.870 --> 00:20:24.450
<i>Everyone taught me that I don't
need to take everything on alone.</i>

00:20:32.100 --> 00:20:35.000
<i>It was all hopeless by myself.</i>

00:20:35.970 --> 00:20:40.560
<i>That is why the story of how "I" became "us"</i>

00:20:44.770 --> 00:20:48.600
<i>surely began the day we met.</i>

00:20:52.490 --> 00:20:55.020
<i>It really took a lot to get here.</i>

00:20:56.180 --> 00:20:59.650
<i>I can't believe this musical
is really almost over.</i>

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:04.240
Hey!

00:21:04.680 --> 00:21:06.910
Are we really okay with
this as the final scene?

00:21:09.990 --> 00:21:12.230
Yeah, I can't accept this!

00:21:12.590 --> 00:21:15.220
I want to sing with everyone at the end!

00:21:15.220 --> 00:21:19.040
I, too, wish for a happy ending
with everyone together.

00:21:19.310 --> 00:21:21.550
Hey, what are you guys doing?

00:21:25.150 --> 00:21:30.760
Dear angels, please save
this pitiful young man!

00:21:32.940 --> 00:21:34.230
We shall grant...

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:36.170
...your wish.

00:21:36.610 --> 00:21:38.320
<i>Macchi? Tsucchi?</i>

00:21:38.320 --> 00:21:39.760
<i>What the heck are they wearing?</i>

00:21:41.540 --> 00:21:43.440
<i>Why do they have the miracle heart lights?!</i>

00:21:45.510 --> 00:21:48.570
Wait, there are more angels here, too!

00:21:52.580 --> 00:21:54.080
Great Angel

00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:56.040
<i>Even Matsuo-senpai and the others?!</i>

00:21:57.210 --> 00:22:00.850
Now, put all your prayers into these lights.

00:22:01.170 --> 00:22:02.670
Put them in!

00:22:05.650 --> 00:22:09.700
Now, make miracles happen with your power!

00:22:09.700 --> 00:22:14.100
Grant new life to this young
man full of friendship!

00:22:16.210 --> 00:22:17.390
Are you surprised?

00:22:17.730 --> 00:22:19.520
I wanted to see your face.

00:22:19.520 --> 00:22:22.110
It's punishment for giving us the run around.

00:22:22.110 --> 00:22:24.670
Come back to life already, Kouta-kun.

00:22:25.130 --> 00:22:27.320
It's best to resign yourself and accept it.

00:22:28.500 --> 00:22:30.640
When the heck did you plan all this?

00:22:37.170 --> 00:22:38.560
Good grief...

00:22:39.170 --> 00:22:40.570
Fine, I'll do it.

00:22:47.070 --> 00:22:49.420
I'd rather be with everyone, too!

00:22:50.150 --> 00:22:51.430
Koural!

00:22:51.430 --> 00:22:52.550
All right!

00:23:13.920 --> 00:23:16.500
I... No,

00:23:17.260 --> 00:23:20.830
we, are sparkling now!

00:23:22.480 --> 00:23:23.280
<i>Yes...</i>

00:23:23.850 --> 00:23:28.090
<i>I'm sure this sparkle is—</i>

00:23:28.880 --> 00:23:30.180
<i>Our youth!</i>

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.060
A stage play version of <i>Sanrio Boys</i>
 has been set for Winter 2018!!

00:23:37.470 --> 00:23:40.060
The details will be announced at a later date! 
Please look forward to it!
